# Project Rules for Cursor

## Canonical specs (read FIRST on every edit)
- /docs/agent-prd.md
- /docs/architecture.md
- /lib/schemas/workout.ts

## Required reply format (for any change)
Cursor MUST produce:
1) Doc-Anchor — list the exact bullets from the above docs that you are applying.
2) Mini spec — 3–7 bullets describing the macro changes and why.
3) Unified patch — one surgical diff only.
4) Self-Check — explicitly confirm:
   - Strict JSON contract enforced; invalid → 400 (no persist).
   - Phases include warmup/strength/accessory/cooldown; strength begins with main/core (except HIIT).
   - Cooldown matches focus muscles (no generic mismatches).
   - Target duration respected (pad or trim as per PRD).
   - No unused imports/vars; TS strict; build passes.
   - Change does not contradict /docs/agent-prd.md or /docs/architecture.md.
5) Files touched — exact list.

## Contracts
- Obey /lib/schemas/workout.ts types and validator in any plan generation or persistence.
- Keep business rules centralized in /lib/workout.ts (main-lift selection, cooldown matching, duration heuristics).

## Engineering constraints
- TypeScript strict; no unused imports/vars.
- Strict JSON from LLM; invalid → HTTP 400.
- UI renders JSON, not free text.
- Equipment from profiles → user_equipment → equipment join.
- Save only on Finish (workout_sessions/workout_sets), with workout_source when available.
- Maintain one active chat_sessions; archive overflow to workout_chat_log.

## Commit/PR messaging
- Reference /docs/agent-prd.md + /docs/architecture.md and summarize the Self-Check in the commit message.
